OpenCMIS Android Client
=======================

The OpenCMIS Android Client provides a collection of methods to access and
manage a CMIS repository from mobile / constrained environments.


OpenCMIS Client Bindings supported
----------------------------------
AtomPub Binding and Browser Binding are supported.
The Web Service Binding (SOAP) is not supported.


Runtime / build notes
---------------------
 - XML uses the shared desktop StAX stack (`XMLConverter` / `XMLUtils` /
   AtomPub SPI) via Woodstox (`com.fasterxml.woodstox:woodstox-core`)
   plus explicit `javax.xml.stream:stax-api` and
   `org.codehaus.woodstox:stax2-api` (Woodstox 7 excludes stax-api
   because the JDK normally provides it; Android does not).
 - The artifact is compiled with `--release 11` (parent reactor stays on
   Java 21). `--release 11` does not prove Android API / DEX
   compatibility by itself; CI also runs a D8 conversion smoke
   (`scripts/android-d8-smoke.sh`, min-api 26). Device/emulator
   instrumentation is still out of scope in this repository.
 - The `pack` ZIP/TAR includes the client JAR plus a `lib/` directory
   with Woodstox, stax-api, and stax2-api. Maven consumers also get
   those as transitive dependencies.
 - Binary pack LICENSE/NOTICE documents third-party licenses. In
   particular, `lib/stax-api-*.jar` (Streaming API for XML / JSR-173,
   `javax.xml.stream:stax-api`) is under the CDDL 1.0 + GPL v2 dual
   license (https://glassfish.dev.java.net/public/CDDL+GPL.html).
   That jar is Category B under the ASF Third-Party License Policy and
   is shipped only in the binary pack (not in the source distribution).
 - Prefer OkHttp for Android sessions
   (`...spi.http.OkHttpHttpInvoker`). The JVM default is Apache
   HttpClient 5; both are available as session parameters.
 - CI runs D8 (min-api 26) and an API 26 emulator smoke that pushes
   the produced DEX onto a running emulator.


IMPORTANT: synchronous API
--------------------------
OpenCMIS Android Client is a SYNCHRONOUS library.
Encapsulate CMIS calls in a background thread (Service, Loader,
Executor, Coroutine, etc.).


Maven dependency
----------------

    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.apache.chemistry.opencmis</groupId>
        <artifactId>chemistry-opencmis-android-client</artifactId>
        <version>${opencmis.version}</version>
    </dependency>

Transitive runtime jars should include Woodstox, stax-api, and stax2-api.
If you shade/minimize, keep `javax.xml.stream` and Woodstox factories.


Build
-----

    mvn -pl chemistry-opencmis-android/chemistry-opencmis-android-client -am package
    ./scripts/android-d8-smoke.sh
